=== General Spriting Guidelines ===

==== Dithering ====
As mentioned in the style section, sprites should use a minimal amount of dithering. Here is an example of too much dithering compared to one with minimal dithering:

https://i.imgur.com/Q1EJDgZ.png

==== Outlining ====
Monster sprites should try using "selective outlining" for your monster's outlines, instead of black lines, like this:    
http://i.imgur.com/Wy2dNeD.png

When creating outlines, you should also try to avoid using "jaggies" in the outline:    
http://i.imgur.com/S2dbRxm.gif

You should also try and avoid using too much anti-aliasing. You only want to use as much AA as is necessary to smooth the edge. If you use too much, the edges can look blurry, and you lose the crispness of the line.
https://i.imgur.com/SQu3W0U.png

These examples come from <code>http://pixeljoint.</code><code>com/forum/forum_posts.asp?TID=11299</code> which has a lot of great spriting tips that recommend these things.